{
 "id": "01a1085d-5357-7763-b586-df70f85be7f4",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (Finance's new accounting tool, adopted late Sept/early Oct 2026, replacing the German-locale tool): plain comma-separated (`,`) and ISO dates `YYYY-MM-DD` (strftime `%Y-%m-%d`). UTF-8 without a BOM. The old tool's semicolon delimiter and DD.MM.YYYY dates no longer apply.",
 "details": "Updated 2026-10-04: user reported Finance moved to a new accounting tool the previous week that wants comma-separated files with ISO dates."
}
